---
description: How to use the ccmcp MCP knowledge base efficiently
alwaysApply: false
---

When a question's answer likely lives in another repo, internal docs, or a
large tree not open in the workspace, use the ccmcp MCP server rather than
grepping:

- `qdrant_list_scopes()` first to discover indexed projects (names/tags).
- `qdrant_find(query, scope)`: omit `scope` to auto-scope to the workspace;
  pass `scope=["proj","tag"]` to target projects; `scope=["*"]` only as a last
  resort — it is the noisiest option.
- Put exact identifiers/flags VERBATIM in the query AND phrase the concept in
  prose (hybrid dense+BM25 search uses both channels).
- Open the returned `source_uri` for full context. If the answer is in an open
  file, read it directly instead of searching.
- `qdrant_store(text, title, session_id)` to persist decisions or summaries
  (TTL-expired, separate artifacts collection).
